@*
    THE organisation-defined obligation form — add / edit.

    One dialog, included by every screen that can author an obligation the
    organisation owns, driven by wwwroot/js/Shared/obligation-form.js.

    WHY IT WAS EXTRACTED
    --------------------
    It lived inline in resolve-workspace.cshtml: ~110 lines of markup and
    ~600 lines of JS -- the type dropdown, the typed rule panel mirrored
    from Control Management, the Assurance -> Automated -> Connection
    cascade, the evidence list, and the save.

    Practice View needs the same form for a practice-level obligation
    (docs/practice-level-obligations.md). Copying it would mean two
    validations, two field lists and two places to change when Control
    Management adds a field -- which is exactly the drift the shared task
    form (_task-form-dialog.cshtml) was created to end. So this is that
    pattern applied a second time.

    ONE FORM, TWO SCOPES
    --------------------
      scope: "instance"  -> POST /practice/api/workflow/resolve/local-obligation
                            the obligation belongs to ONE practice instance
                            (migration 227), unchanged behaviour
      scope: "practice"  -> POST /practice/api/practice-obligations
                            the obligation belongs to the PRACTICE and fans
                            out to every instance of it

    The caller says which; nothing else about the form differs. The two
    endpoints take the same field set because the practice-level table
    mirrors the instance-level columns on purpose.

    SELF-CONTAINED STYLES, AND WHY THE CLASSES WERE RENAMED
    -------------------------------------------------------
    The inline version borrowed from two places: global `.rw-dialog*`
    rules AND `#rwRoot`-scoped ones (`.rw-note`, `.rw-typed`,
    `.rw-freq-actions`). Inside the Operationalize page that worked,
    because the dialog sat inside `#rwRoot`. On Practice View (`#pvRoot`)
    half the form would have rendered unstyled.

    So every class here is `gof-` prefixed and defined below. The dialog
    looks the same on any page that includes it, and nothing in it can
    reach another dialog.

    NOT A <form>
    ------------
    A `<form method="dialog">` submits on Enter in any text input, which
    closes the dialog and throws the half-typed obligation away. Every
    button is type="button" and the save is a fetch, so form semantics buy
    nothing here. Same reason the inline version used a div.

    No backdrop dismissal either: half-filled work should not vanish on a
    stray click, so Cancel is the only way out.

    Included ONCE per page. The ids are global, which is what lets any
    screen on that page open the same dialog.
*@
<dialog class="gof" id="gofDialog" aria-labelledby="gofHeading">
  <div class="gof-form">
    <header class="gof-head">
        <h2 id="gofHeading">Add obligation</h2>
        <button class="pm-icon-button" id="gofClose" type="button" aria-label="Close">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i>
        </button>
    </header>

    <div class="gof-body">
        @* 0 on an add; the row id on an edit. The server echoes the id it
           wrote back into here even on a failed save, so a retry updates
           that obligation instead of inserting a second one. *@
        <input type="hidden" id="gofId" value="0">

        <div class="gof-fields">
            <div class="full"><label>Obligation name
                <input type="text" id="gofName" maxlength="500" placeholder="What must be done, or be true">
            </label></div>
            <div class="full"><label>Description
                <textarea id="gofDescription" rows="2"></textarea>
            </label></div>
            <div><label>Type
                <select id="gofType"><option value="">Select a type...</option></select>
            </label></div>
        </div>

        @* The rule fields are not written here: they are built from the
           chosen type's field list, which the API reads out of Control
           Management's own table for that type. So the form asks for
           exactly what CM asks for, and a column CM adds appears here with
           no change on this side. *@
        <div id="gofRuleBox" hidden>
            <p class="gof-note" id="gofRuleNote"></p>
            <div class="gof-fields" id="gofRuleFields"></div>
        </div>

        @* Execution frequency is deliberately absent from this row: it is
           a field of the Execution type and shows on the typed panel above
           for that type only. Asking again here asked twice for Execution
           and asked a meaningless question for everything else. The value
           still flows into execution_frequency_id on save.

           Responsibility reads as Owner (migration 244). Approval
           authority is hidden -- the control, its column and its save-path
           plumbing all remain, it simply does not render. *@
        <div class="gof-fields">
            <div><label>Name of the Person
                <select id="gofResponsibility"><option value="">Not set</option></select>
            </label></div>
            <div hidden><label>Approval authority
                <select id="gofApproval"><option value="">Not set</option></select>
            </label></div>
            <div id="gofAssuranceTypeWrap" hidden><label>Assurance type
                <select id="gofAssuranceType"><option value="">Not set</option></select>
            </label></div>
            <div id="gofConnectionTypeWrap" hidden><label>Connection type
                <select id="gofConnectionType"><option value="">Not set</option></select>
            </label></div>
            <div id="gofConnectionUrlWrap" class="full" hidden><label>Connection URL
                <input type="text" id="gofConnectionUrl" placeholder="https://..." />
            </label></div>
            <div id="gofImplStatusWrap"><label>Implementation status
                <select id="gofImplStatus"><option value="">Not set</option></select>
            </label></div>
            <div class="full"><label>Remarks
                <textarea id="gofRemarks" rows="2"></textarea>
            </label></div>
        </div>

        @* Evidence for this obligation (migration 232). Adopting a
           published obligation creates its evidence from what the
           authority published; an organisation-defined one has no
           authority behind it, so it is declared here. *@
        <div class="gof-typed" id="gofEvidenceBox">
            <h4>Evidence</h4>
            <p class="gof-note" id="gofEvidenceNote">
                What proves this obligation has been met. Location and owner are
                filled in later, on the card.
            </p>
            <div id="gofEvidenceRows"></div>
            <div class="gof-fields" style="margin-top:8px">
                <div><label>Add evidence type
                    <select id="gofEvidencePick"><option value="">Select a type...</option></select>
                </label></div>
                <div class="gof-inline-actions">
                    <button class="pm-button ghost small" id="gofEvidenceAdd" type="button">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> Add
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <footer class="gof-foot">
        <button class="pm-button" id="gofSave" type="button">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> Save obligation
        </button>
        <button class="pm-button ghost" id="gofCancel" type="button">Cancel</button>
        <span class="gof-note" id="gofMsg"></span>
    </footer>
  </div>
</dialog>

<style>
    /* Scoped to .gof so nothing here can reach another dialog, and so the
       dialog does not depend on the page it was included on. */

    /* Sized to the form rather than the viewport: a short type (Constraint
       has one rule field) should not open a full-height sheet. */
    .gof {
        width: min(880px, calc(100vw - 32px));
        max-height: calc(100vh - 64px);
        padding: 0; border: 0; border-radius: 10px;
        background: #fff; color: var(--grac-ink, #25345a);
    }
    .gof::backdrop { background: rgba(15, 23, 42, .45); }

    .gof-form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; max-height: calc(100vh - 64px); }

    .gof-head {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
        padding: 12px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grac-line, #e2e7f0);
    }
    .gof-head h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; flex: 1 1 auto; }

    /* The only part that scrolls, so the actions stay reachable however
       long the typed panel gets. */
    .gof-body { padding: 14px 16px; overflow-y: auto; }

    .gof-foot {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
        padding: 12px 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--grac-line, #e2e7f0);
        background: #f8fafc;
    }

    .gof-fields {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(190px, 1fr));
        gap: 10px 14px;
    }
    .gof-fields + .gof-fields, .gof-fields + #gofRuleBox { margin-top: 12px; }
    .gof-fields .full { grid-column: 1 / -1; }

    .gof label { display: block; font-size: 12px; color: var(--grac-muted, #758095); }
    .gof label > select,
    .gof label > input,
    .gof label > textarea {
        display: block; width: 100%; margin-top: 3px;
        font-size: 13px; color: var(--grac-ink, #25345a);
        padding: 4px 6px;
        border: 1px solid var(--grac-line, #e2e7f0); border-radius: 5px;
        background: #fff; font-family: inherit;
    }
    .gof label > textarea { resize: vertical; }
    .gof .required { color: #b91c1c; }
    .gof-note { font-size: 11px; color: var(--grac-muted, #758095); margin: 0; }

    /* The typed panel and the evidence block: separated from the fields
       above by a rule rather than by whitespace alone, because both are a
       different KIND of question -- one is the obligation's own rule, the
       other is what will prove it. */
    #gofRuleBox, .gof-typed {
        margin-top: 14px; padding-top: 12px;
        border-top: 1px dashed var(--grac-line, #e2e7f0);
    }
    #gofRuleBox .gof-note { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .gof-typed h4 {
        margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--grac-muted, #758095);
    }

    /* A button that has to line up with the bottom edge of the select
       beside it, which sits under its own label. */
    .gof-inline-actions {
        display: flex; align-items: end; gap: 8px; padding-bottom: 1px;
    }

    .gof-evidence-line {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;
        padding: 6px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--grac-line, #e2e7f0);
    }
    .gof-evidence-line:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .gof-evidence-line .gof-evidence-name { flex: 1 1 160px; font-size: 13px; }
    /* An inline label inside an evidence row is a control beside its text,
       not a stacked field -- so it opts out of the block rule above. */
    .gof-evidence-line label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; }
    .gof-evidence-line label > input { display: inline-block; width: auto; margin-top: 0; }
    .gof-evidence-line .gof-evidence-retention { flex: 0 1 170px; display: block; }
    .gof-evidence-line .gof-evidence-retention > input { display: block; width: 100%; margin-top: 3px; }
    /* The evidence Description drops onto its own full-width line beneath the
       type/mandatory/retention row (the line is flex-wrap), so a longer note
       gets the dialog's width instead of fighting the controls for space. */
    .gof-evidence-line .gof-evidence-desc { flex: 1 1 100%; display: block; }
    .gof-evidence-line .gof-evidence-desc > textarea {
        display: block; width: 100%; margin-top: 3px; resize: vertical;
    }

    /* One column on a narrow window: below this the auto-fit pairs stop
       helping and start cramping. */
    @@media (max-width: 720px) {
        .gof-fields { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    }
</style>
